This directory includes two primary run scripts. File gchp.run was developed at WashU
for running multi-node GCHP runs. It utilizes script execute.sh. File
gchp.run_from_most_recent_checkpoint_date.run was developed at Harvard for
running single-node GCHP Jacobian runs with the Integrated Methane Inversion.
The former assumes a specific AMI. The latter can be used with any AMI that has
a gchp.env file that loads libraries needed for GCHP.

File gchp.submit_consecutive_jobs.sh allows submitting multiple GCHP jobs as
sequential dependencies. This is useful for splitting up a run in time. Edit the
file to submit the primary run script you wish to use.

Files that start with gchp.build.* are for building GCHP with either the fullchem
or carbon chemistry mechanism. These scripts are useful for submitting GCHP build
to an instance with more cores and greater memory than the head node.

File sample_pcluster.yaml is a simple pcluster yaml file for creating a pcluster.
See GEOS-Chem on AWS documentation for more information, accessible via GC-Classic
and GCHP ReadTheDocs.

Notes:

Use only physical cores on AWS. Do not use multi-threading. Disable multi-threading
in yaml file when creating a pcluster.

On AWS with EFA (used for multi-node GCHP runs) it might be necessary to turn on
WRITE_RESTART_BY_OSERVER and set numbers of O-servers in GCHP.rc to 6 to avoid
crashes when writing restart files. See discussion in
https://github.com/geoschem/GCHP/issues/493.

